      <h1 id="migrating-frr-k8s-resources" class="group scroll-mt-20">Migrating FRR-K8s resources<a href="#migrating-frr-k8s-resources" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Migrating FRR-K8s custom resources is required when upgrading from OpenShift Container Platform 4.17 or earlier with the MetalLB Operator deployed. Existing FRRConfiguration resources in the <code>metallb-system</code> namespace must be moved to the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace to align with the updated architecture. Learn how to migrate these resources using the CLI and how to verify that the migration completed successfully.</p>
      <p>All user-created FRR-K8s custom resources (CRs) in the <code>metallb-system</code> namespace under OpenShift Container Platform 4.17 and earlier releases must be migrated to the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace. As a cluster administrator, you can migrate your FRR-K8s custom resources to the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace using the CLI.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-bgp-frr-k8s-migration_migrating-frr-k8s-resources" class="group scroll-mt-20">Migrating FRR-K8s resources<a href="#nw-bgp-frr-k8s-migration_migrating-frr-k8s-resources" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can migrate the FRR-K8s <code>FRRConfiguration</code> custom resources from the <code>metallb-system</code> namespace to the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace.</p>
      <p>When upgrading from an earlier version of OpenShift Container Platform with the Metal LB Operator deployed, you must manually migrate your custom <code>FRRConfiguration</code> configurations from the <code>metallb-system</code> namespace to the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You are logged in to the cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      To create the <code>openshift-frr-k8s</code> namespace, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create namespace openshift-frr-k8s"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To automate the migration, create a shell script named <code>migrate.sh</code> with the following contents:
      <CodeBlock code={"#!/bin/bash\nOLD_NAMESPACE=\"metallb-system\"\nNEW_NAMESPACE=\"openshift-frr-k8s\"\nFILTER_OUT=\"metallb-\"\noc get frrconfigurations.frrk8s.metallb.io -n \"${OLD_NAMESPACE}\" -o json |\\\n  jq -r '.items[] | select(.metadata.name | test(\"'\"${FILTER_OUT}\"'\") | not)' |\\\n  jq -r '.metadata.namespace = \"'\"${NEW_NAMESPACE}\"'\"' |\\\n  oc create -f -"} lang="bash" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To execute the migration, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ bash migrate.sh"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To confirm that the migration succeeded, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get frrconfigurations.frrk8s.metallb.io -n openshift-frr-k8s"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p>After the migration is complete, you can remove the <code>FRRConfiguration</code> custom resources from the <code>metallb-system</code> namespace.</p>
